From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: ggml-cuda: tensor-core MTP verify scan

The MTP verify step of the ReplaySSM scan computed C_i.h0 and C_i.B_k as FP32
dot products with warp reductions, reading the committed B and x cache rows
from global memory inside them: instruction-bound on the CUDA cores.
ssm_replay_verify_tc replaces it: it stages only the C rows of the tokens and
the B and x rows of the window in shared memory, four values per load, and
computes both products as F16 mma.sync with F32 accumulation (the checkpoint
and the cache rows are F16 already). The tensor-core kernel needs SM80 or
newer.

Upstream: not planned (Nemotron-H MTP verify path).

